module ctcDetection
module viabilityDetection
module her2FISHDetection

manifest WholeBlood
manifest RBCLysisBuffer
manifest PBS
manifest EDTA_BSA_Buffer
manifest MCF7_Cells
manifest T24_Cells
manifest SheathFluid
manifest Paraformaldehyde
manifest TritonX100
manifest PanCytokeratinFITC
manifest CD45_APC
manifest Hoechst
manifest PropidiumIodide
manifest RNase
manifest Formamide_SSC
manifest SSC_Wash
manifest HER2_FISHProbe
manifest DAPI

instructions:

// ============================================================
// An Ultra-High-Throughput Spiral Microfluidic Biochip for
// the Enrichment of Circulating Tumor Cells
// Warkiani, Khoo, Tan, Bhagat, Lim, Yap, Lee, Soo,
// Han, Lim -- Analyst, 2014, 139, 3245-3255
// DOI: 10.1039/c4an00355a
//
// Platform: Multiplexed spiral microfluidic biochip
//   (3 stacked single-layer PDMS spiral chips, each with
//   2 inlets and 2 outlets). Fabricated by standard SU-8
//   lithography and PDMS soft lithography (1:10 ratio,
//   cured 80 C, 1-2 h). Device bonded onto a microscopic
//   glass slide by air plasma.
//
// Separation principle: Inertial focusing + Dean drag forces
//   inside rectangular-cross-section spiral microchannels.
//   CTCs (>15 um) equilibrate near inner wall; smaller
//   hematological cells (RBCs, WBCs, platelets, <20 um)
//   migrate to outer wall under Dean vortex influence,
//   enabling label-free, size-based separation at dual outlet.
//
// Key performance metrics:
//   Throughput:   7.5 mL blood in <10 min (multiplexed)
//   Sensitivity:  100% (10/10 patient samples positive)
//   WBC depletion: ~99.99% (from ~7e6 nucleated cells)
//   Purity:       1 CTC per 30-100 WBCs (~4 log depletion)
//   Recovery:     20-135 CTCs/mL (breast and lung patients)
//   Cell viability: >90% (PI staining, <10% dead)
//   Recovery efficiency: 87.6% MCF-7; 76.4% T24 (spiked)
//   Sample flow rate: 350 uL/min; Sheath: 750 uL/min
//   Sample concentration: 2x (7.5 mL -> 3.75 mL)
//
// NOTE ON FLOW ABSTRACTION: `mix` statements abstract
//   continuous-flow microfluidic channel events (cell loading,
//   hydrodynamic focusing, Dean vortex separation) rather than
//   DMF electrode mixing. This is consistent with the
//   abstraction used in samlali_hybrid_microfluidics_isoclone.bs
//   for channel-based trapping and encapsulation events.
//
// NOTE ON RBC LYSIS: Whole blood is lysed with ammonium
//   chloride RBC lysis buffer before on-chip processing.
//   Removes RBCs, concentrates nucleated cells 2x for faster
//   processing. Cell loss not significant (98% recovery,
//   p=0.82). Lysis does not alter cell morphology (p=0.2).
//
// NOTE ON DURATION TOKENS: BioScript supports s and m only.
//   All paper durations converted accordingly.
//   Overnight hybridization (42 C) approximated as 600m (10 h).
//
// NOTE ON CELL CULTURE PRE-INCUBATION (FIX #8):
//   MCF-7 and T24 cells are cultured in DMEM + 10% FBS +
//   1% pen-strep at 37 C / 5% CO2 until 80% confluence before
//   spiking. Following samlali convention, this is modelled as
//   heat at 37c for 2880m (48 h representative culture period)
//   applied to the cell manifests before resuspension in
//   EDTA_BSA_Buffer. Trypsin/EDTA dissociation is abstracted
//   into the same heat step.
//
// THREE PROTOCOLS encoded in sequence:
//
//   PROTOCOL 1 (BB1-BB4): MCF-7 recovery efficiency experiment.
//     Fresh healthy donor blood -> RBC lysis -> MCF-7 spike
//     -> spiral chip separation -> ctcDetection QC gate.
//     Expected: 87.6% recovery efficiency (Fig. 4A).
//
//   PROTOCOL 2 (BB5-BB8): T24 cell viability experiment.
//     Fresh healthy donor blood (independent from Protocol 1)
//     -> RBC lysis -> T24 spike -> spiral chip separation ->
//     PI staining + pan-CK/CD45 staining -> viabilityDetection
//     QC gate. Expected: <10% PI+ (high viability) (Fig. 4B).
//
//   PROTOCOL 3 (BB9-BB14): Clinical CTC enrichment from
//     patient blood. Fresh clinical blood -> RBC lysis ->
//     spiral chip separation -> PFA fixation -> Triton X-100
//     permeabilization -> IF staining (Pan-CK/CD45/Hoechst) ->
//     ctcDetection QC gate -> HER2 FISH (pass branch only).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main            -- entry: MCF-7 culture, blood prep,
//                           RBC lysis, spike, on-chip separation
//   BB2  mcf7Pass        -- ctcSignal > 0: CTCs recovered, dispose
//   BB3  mcf7Fail        -- ctcSignal <= 0: no CTCs, drain
//   BB4  mcf7Join        -- join: T24 viability protocol begins
//   BB5  viabSep         -- fresh blood, T24 spike, on-chip sep,
//                           fixation, PI + pan-CK/CD45 staining
//   BB6  viabPass        -- viabilitySignal > 0: viable, dispose
//   BB7  viabFail        -- viabilitySignal <= 0: low viab, drain
//   BB8  viabJoin        -- join: clinical protocol begins
//   BB9  clinSep         -- clinical blood, lysis, on-chip sep,
//                           PFA fixation, permeabilization, IF
//   BB10 clinPass        -- clinicalSignal > 0: CTCs detected,
//                           proceed to HER2 FISH
//   BB11 clinFail        -- clinicalSignal <= 0: no CTCs, drain
//   BB12 finalCleanup    -- terminal: dispose QC signal, end
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// PROTOCOL 1 -- MCF-7 spiked recovery efficiency experiment
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Culture MCF-7 cells prior to spiking.
//   MCF-7 (breast adenocarcinoma, HTB-22, ATCC, ~20 um diam.)
//   cultured in high-glucose DMEM + 10% FBS + 1% pen-strep
//   at 37 C / 5% CO2 until 80% confluence. Sub-cultivated
//   1:3 twice a week. Media replaced every 48 h.
//   Dissociated with 0.01% trypsin / 5.3 mM EDTA (Lonza).
//   FIX #8: Cell culture pre-incubation modelled as heat
//   at 37c for 2880m (48 h), consistent with samlali.bs.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

mcf7Cells       = dispense 1 units of MCF7_Cells
heat mcf7Cells at 37c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Resuspend MCF-7 in EDTA+BSA buffer.
//   Cells resuspended in PBS + 2 mM EDTA + 0.5% BSA
//   (Miltenyi Biotec, Germany) to prevent non-specific
//   adsorption on tubing and microchannel walls.
//   Spike concentration: 500 cells per 7.5 mL whole blood.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

edtaBsaBuffer   = dispense 1 units of EDTA_BSA_Buffer
mcf7Resuspended = mix mcf7Cells with edtaBsaBuffer for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Prepare healthy donor blood and perform RBC lysis.
//   7.5 mL whole blood collected in Vacutainer EDTA tubes
//   (Becton-Dickinson, NJ, USA). Processed within 2-4 h.
//   Lysed with ammonium chloride RBC lysis buffer (Bioscience,
//   USA) for 5 min at RT under continuous gentle mixing.
//   Centrifuged at 1000xg for 5 min (modelled as heat at 25c).
//   Nucleated cell pellet resuspended in PBS. Concentrated
//   to 3.75 mL (2x) for optimal on-chip WBC input (~14e6).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wholeBlood1     = dispense 1 units of WholeBlood
rbcLysis1       = dispense 1 units of RBCLysisBuffer
lysedBlood1     = mix wholeBlood1 with rbcLysis1 for 5m

// Centrifugation at 1000xg, 5 min (no centrifuge primitive;
// modelled as heat at 25c for 5m per compiler convention).
heat lysedBlood1 at 25c for 5m

pbs1            = dispense 1 units of PBS
nucleated1      = mix lysedBlood1 with pbs1 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Spike MCF-7 cells into nucleated cell fraction.
//   500 MCF-7 cells spiked into the 7.5 mL nucleated fraction
//   at clinically relevant concentration for recovery testing.
//   MCF-7 and T24 are spiked in separate, independent
//   experiments (not co-spiked). (FIX #2)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

spikedMcf7      = mix nucleated1 with mcf7Resuspended for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: On-chip separation -- MCF-7 spiked sample.
//   Nucleated fraction (2x concentrated, 3.75 mL) loaded at
//   sample inlet. PBS sheath fluid at sheath inlet.
//   Sample: 350 uL/min; Sheath: 750 uL/min; ~10 min total.
//   Dean vortex + inertial lift: CTCs to inner wall (CTC
//   outlet); WBCs/RBCs/platelets to outer wall (waste outlet).
//   Enrichment: ~10^4-fold from nucleated cell fraction.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts channel-based hydrodynamic separation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sheath1         = dispense 1 units of SheathFluid
mcf7Separated   = mix spikedMcf7 with sheath1 for 10m

ctcSignal       = detect ctcDetection on mcf7Separated for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: MCF-7 Recovery QC gate
// Pass (BB2): ctcSignal > 0 -> CTCs recovered at CTC outlet.
//   Expected recovery: 87.6% for MCF-7 at 500 cells/7.5 mL.
//   Identified by pan-CK+/CD45- immunofluorescence (Fig. 4A).
// Fail (BB3): ctcSignal <= 0 -> no CTCs detected; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (mcf7Join).
// ============================================================

if (ctcSignal > 0) {
    dispose mcf7Separated
} else {
    drain mcf7Separated
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: mcf7Join
// Dispose MCF-7 QC signal. T24 viability protocol begins.
// ============================================================

dispose ctcSignal

// ============================================================
// BB5: viabSep
// PROTOCOL 2 -- T24 cell viability experiment
// Independent fresh blood sample; independent T24 culture.
// (FIX #1: T24 viability arm now uses its own WholeBlood
//  dispense and lysis sequence, not nucleated1 from Protocol 1
//  which was already consumed by spikedMcf7.)
// (FIX #2: MCF-7 and T24 are fully independent experiments.)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Culture T24 cells prior to viability spiking.
//   T24 (bladder carcinoma, HTB-4, ATCC, ~30 um diameter).
//   Same culture conditions as MCF-7 (DMEM + 10% FBS +
//   1% pen-strep, 37 C / 5% CO2, 80% confluence).
//   FIX #8: Pre-incubation modelled as heat at 37c for 2880m.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

t24Cells        = dispense 1 units of T24_Cells
heat t24Cells at 37c for 2880m

edtaBsa2        = dispense 1 units of EDTA_BSA_Buffer
t24Resuspended  = mix t24Cells with edtaBsa2 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Prepare fresh healthy donor blood for viability arm.
//   Independent 7.5 mL blood sample (separate from Protocol 1).
//   Same RBC lysis and PBS resuspension as STEP 3.
//   A known concentration of T24 cells spiked into whole blood
//   before lysis; T24 counts compared before and after lysis
//   to quantify cell loss incurred by the lysis step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wholeBlood2     = dispense 1 units of WholeBlood
rbcLysis2       = dispense 1 units of RBCLysisBuffer
lysedBlood2     = mix wholeBlood2 with rbcLysis2 for 5m

heat lysedBlood2 at 25c for 5m

pbs2            = dispense 1 units of PBS
nucleated2      = mix lysedBlood2 with pbs2 for 1m

spikedT24       = mix nucleated2 with t24Resuspended for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: On-chip separation -- T24 spiked viability sample.
//   Same spiral biochip parameters as STEP 5.
//   CTC outlet fraction collected; viability assessed
//   immediately after retrieval.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sheath2         = dispense 1 units of SheathFluid
t24Separated    = mix spikedT24 with sheath2 for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: Viability staining -- PI + pan-CK/CD45 panel.
//   FIX #3: The paper's viability assay uses BOTH PI staining
//   (to identify dead cells, ex 488/em 617 nm) AND pan-CK/CD45
//   IF staining (to confirm recovered cells are cancer cells,
//   not contaminating WBCs). Both reagents are now included.
//   Outlet samples fixed with 4% PFA for 10 min at RT.
//   Permeabilized with 0.1% Triton X-100 in PBS.
//   FIX #4: PFA fixation and Triton X-100 permeabilization
//   are now explicitly represented with their own manifests
//   and mix/heat steps, matching the paper's IF protocol.
//   Antibody cocktail: pan-CK FITC (1:100) + APC-CD45 (1:100)
//   + Hoechst + PI in PBS buffer, 30 min on ice.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Fixation: 4% paraformaldehyde (PFA), 10 min at RT (25 C).
pfa1            = dispense 1 units of Paraformaldehyde
t24Fixed        = mix t24Separated with pfa1 for 10m
heat t24Fixed at 25c for 10m

// Permeabilization: 0.1% Triton X-100 in PBS, brief wash.
triton1         = dispense 1 units of TritonX100
pbs3            = dispense 1 units of PBS
tritonPbs1      = mix triton1 with pbs3 for 1m
t24Permeabilized = mix t24Fixed with tritonPbs1 for 5m

// Staining cocktail: pan-CK FITC + APC-CD45 + Hoechst + PI.
panCK1          = dispense 1 units of PanCytokeratinFITC
cd45Ab1         = dispense 1 units of CD45_APC
hoechst1        = dispense 1 units of Hoechst
piStain         = dispense 1 units of PropidiumIodide

viabStainMix1   = mix panCK1 with cd45Ab1 for 1m
viabStainMix2   = mix viabStainMix1 with hoechst1 for 1m
viabStainFull   = mix viabStainMix2 with piStain for 1m

stainedViability = mix t24Permeabilized with viabStainFull for 30m

// Incubation on ice (4 C) for 30 min (paper: antibody
// cocktail + Hoechst in PBS buffer, 30 min on ice).
heat stainedViability at 4c for 30m

// Viability detection: <10% PI+ cells = high viability.
// Quantified by BD Accuri C6 flow cytometer; cells gated
// on forward/side scatter and fluorescence intensity.
viabilitySignal = detect viabilityDetection on stainedViability for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB6 / BB7: Viability QC gate
// Pass (BB6): viabilitySignal > 0 -> <10% PI+ (high viability,
//   >90% viable). Neither lysis nor spiral shear significantly
//   impacts cell viability (p=0.6687 vs control, N=3).
// Fail (BB7): viabilitySignal <= 0 -> >10% PI+ (low viability;
//   lysis or shear damage); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB8 (viabJoin).
// ============================================================

if (viabilitySignal > 0) {
    dispose stainedViability
} else {
    drain stainedViability
}

// ============================================================
// BB8: viabJoin
// Dispose viability QC signal. Clinical protocol begins.
// ============================================================

dispose viabilitySignal

// ============================================================
// BB9: clinSep
// PROTOCOL 3 -- Clinical CTC enrichment from patient blood
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: Collect clinical blood sample.
//   7.5 mL whole blood from Stage IV metastatic breast or
//   lung cancer patient. Collected in Vacutainer EDTA tubes.
//   Processed within 2-4 h to prevent blood coagulation.
//   10 patient samples total (5 breast cancer, 5 NSCLC).
//   5 healthy donor samples used as controls.
//   IRB-approved protocol (Institutional Review Board).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

clinicalBlood   = dispense 1 units of WholeBlood

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11: RBC lysis of clinical sample.
//   Same ammonium chloride lysis protocol as STEP 3.
//   7.5 mL lysed, centrifuged at 1000xg for 5 min, resuspended
//   in PBS and concentrated to 3.75 mL (2x) for on-chip input.
//   Optimal WBC input: ~14e6 WBCs (2x concentration selected
//   by characterisation experiments, Fig. 2B).
//   Input velocity: 350 uL/min sample, 750 uL/min sheath.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rbcLysis3       = dispense 1 units of RBCLysisBuffer
clinLysed       = mix clinicalBlood with rbcLysis3 for 5m

heat clinLysed at 25c for 5m

pbs4            = dispense 1 units of PBS
clinNucleated   = mix clinLysed with pbs4 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 12: On-chip separation of clinical sample.
//   Multiplexed spiral biochip (3 stacked chips):
//   Sample: 350 uL/min; Sheath: 750 uL/min; ~10 min total.
//   CTCs (15-35 um, pan-CK+/CD45-) collected at inner outlet.
//   WBCs (12-15 um, CD45+) exit at waste outlet.
//   WBC depletion: ~99.99% from 7e6 input nucleated cells.
//   Robustness confirmed: ~900-1200 WBCs collected/5 min
//   uniformly across 0-30 min processing window (Fig. 2C).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sheath3         = dispense 1 units of SheathFluid
clinSeparated   = mix clinNucleated with sheath3 for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 13: PFA fixation and Triton X-100 permeabilization.
//   FIX #4: Fixation and permeabilization now explicitly
//   encoded as separate steps with their own manifests,
//   matching the paper's IF staining protocol (Section 2.3).
//   CTC outlet fraction fixed with 4% PFA for 10 min at RT.
//   Permeabilized with 0.1% Triton X-100 in PBS.
//   These steps are required before antibody staining for
//   intracellular pan-cytokeratin detection.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Fixation: 4% PFA, 10 min at RT (25 C).
pfa2            = dispense 1 units of Paraformaldehyde
clinFixed       = mix clinSeparated with pfa2 for 10m
heat clinFixed at 25c for 10m

// Permeabilization: 0.1% Triton X-100 in PBS.
triton2         = dispense 1 units of TritonX100
pbs5            = dispense 1 units of PBS
tritonPbs2      = mix triton2 with pbs5 for 1m
clinPermeabilized = mix clinFixed with tritonPbs2 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 14: Immunofluorescence (IF) staining for CTC ID.
//   Staining panel (Miltenyi Biotec Asia Pacific, Singapore):
//     - Hoechst (DNA, nuclear counterstain)
//     - Pan-cytokeratin-FITC antibody (1:100, epithelial marker)
//     - APC-conjugated anti-CD45 antibody (1:100, WBC marker)
//   Incubated 30 min on ice in PBS buffer.
//   CTC scoring: Hoechst+ / Pan-CK+ / CD45-
//   Imaged by epi-fluorescence microscopy and/or BD Accuri C6.
//   Cells gated on forward/side scatter and fluorescence.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

panCK2          = dispense 1 units of PanCytokeratinFITC
cd45Ab2         = dispense 1 units of CD45_APC
hoechst2        = dispense 1 units of Hoechst

ifStainMix      = mix panCK2 with cd45Ab2 for 1m
ifStainFull     = mix ifStainMix with hoechst2 for 1m

stainedClinical = mix clinPermeabilized with ifStainFull for 30m
heat stainedClinical at 4c for 30m

clinicalSignal  = detect ctcDetection on stainedClinical for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB10 / BB11: Clinical CTC detection QC gate
// Pass (BB10): clinicalSignal > 0 -> CTCs detected
//   (Hoechst+/Pan-CK+/CD45-). Proceed to HER2 FISH.
//   Expected counts: 20-67 CTCs/mL (breast cancer, n=5);
//   33-135 CTCs/mL (lung cancer, n=5). 100% detection (10/10).
//   Healthy donor background: 1-4 CK+ cells/mL (controls).
// Fail (BB11): clinicalSignal <= 0 -> no CTCs above threshold;
//   drain (consistent with healthy donor control result).
// Both branches converge at BB12 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (clinicalSignal > 0) {

    // ----------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 15: HER2 FISH analysis on isolated CTCs.
    //   Performed on HER2+ breast cancer patient samples (n=5).
    //   Paper protocol (Section 2.4 - DNA fluorescence FISH):
    //
    //   (a) Cytospin onto slides (600 rpm, 6 min).
    //   (b) Fix in 4% PFA, 10 min RT.
    //   (c) Dehydrate via ethanol series (80%, 90%, 100%).
    //   (d) RNase treatment: 4 mg/mL, 40 min at 37 C.
    //       FIX #6: RNase step now explicitly encoded.
    //   (e) Denature: 70% formamide/2xSSC, 80 C, 10 min.
    //       FIX #5: 80 C denaturation step now encoded.
    //   (f) Hybridize HER2 probe (HER-2/neu gene locus, red)
    //       + CEP17 (chr.17 centromere, green) at 42 C overnight.
    //       Approximated as 600m (10 h) per BioScript s/m limit.
    //   (g) Post-hybridization wash: 50% formamide/2xSSC then
    //       2xSSC at 45 C under shaking.
    //       FIX #7: Wash steps at 45 C now explicitly encoded.
    //   (h) DAPI counterstain; coverslip (50x50 mm, Fisher).
    //
    //   HER2 amplification criterion: HER2/CEP17 ratio > 2
    //   in single nuclei.
    //   Result: 3 of 5 HER2+ patients showed HER2-negative CTCs
    //   (HER2/CEP17 < 2), indicating CTC heterogeneity vs.
    //   primary tumor (Fig. 5C).
    //
    //   NOTE ON REAGENT MANIFESTS: Formamide_SSC encodes
    //   70% formamide/2xSSC (denaturation, step e) and
    //   50% formamide/2xSSC (post-hybridization wash, step g).
    //   SSC_Wash encodes the 2xSSC final wash (step g).
    //   Both are separately dispensed at their respective steps.
    // ----------------------------------------------------------

    her2Probe       = dispense 1 units of HER2_FISHProbe
    dapiStain       = dispense 1 units of DAPI

    // (b+c) Fixation (4% PFA, 10 min RT) and ethanol
    //   dehydration series (80%, 90%, 100%) -- abstracted as
    //   a single heat step at 25c for 10m (RT processing).
    pfa3            = dispense 1 units of Paraformaldehyde
    fishFixed       = mix stainedClinical with pfa3 for 10m
    heat fishFixed at 25c for 10m

    // (d) RNase treatment: 4 mg/mL RNase in PBS/0.2% Tween 20,
    //   40 min at 37 C. Removes RNA to prevent non-specific
    //   probe binding. FIX #6.
    rnase           = dispense 1 units of RNase
    rnaseTreated    = mix fishFixed with rnase for 40m
    heat rnaseTreated at 37c for 40m

    // (e) Denaturation: 70% formamide/2xSSC, 80 C, 10 min.
    //   Denatures double-stranded DNA to allow probe access.
    //   FIX #5.
    formamideSsc    = dispense 1 units of Formamide_SSC
    denatured       = mix rnaseTreated with formamideSsc for 10m
    heat denatured at 80c for 10m

    // (f) Probe hybridization: HER2 + CEP17 probes applied
    //   directly to slides at 42 C overnight (approximated
    //   as 600m = 10 h per BioScript s/m constraint).
    //   Dark and humid conditions throughout.
    her2ProbeMix    = mix denatured with her2Probe for 1m
    heat her2ProbeMix at 42c for 600m

    // (g) Post-hybridization washes.
    //   Wash 1: 50% formamide/2xSSC at 45 C under shaking.
    //   Wash 2: 2xSSC at 45 C under shaking.
    //   FIX #7: Wash steps now explicitly encoded.
    formamideWash   = dispense 1 units of Formamide_SSC
    sscWash         = dispense 1 units of SSC_Wash

    washed1         = mix her2ProbeMix with formamideWash for 5m
    heat washed1 at 45c for 5m

    washed2         = mix washed1 with sscWash for 5m
    heat washed2 at 45c for 5m

    // (h) DAPI counterstain; coverslip (50x50 mm).
    dapiMix         = mix washed2 with dapiStain for 5m

    her2Signal      = detect her2FISHDetection on dapiMix for 30s

    dispose dapiMix
    dispose her2Signal

} else {
    drain stainedClinical
}

// ============================================================
// BB12: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose clinical CTC QC signal. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose clinicalSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
